# solarized-dark — Solarized, dark, by Ethan Schoonover.
#
# Upstream: https://github.com/altercation/solarized
# Licence:  MIT
#
# The oldest palette here and still the most deliberate: its sixteen values were
# chosen for fixed CIELAB relationships rather than by eye, which is why the
# eight accents are shared UNCHANGED between the light and dark variants. That
# is also why it reads calmer than anything else in this directory -- its chroma
# is low by construction, not by taste.

# -- neutrals: the base03..base1 monotone ramp ------------------------------
COOL_BG0=#002B36          # base03
COOL_BG1=#073642          # base02
COOL_BG2=#586E75          # base01
COOL_FG0=#93A1A1          # base1
COOL_FG1=#839496          # base0
COOL_DIM=#839496          # base0
COOL_DIMMER=#586E75       # base01
# -- the ramp: cyan -> blue -> violet -> magenta -> orange ------------------
COOL_0=#2AA198
COOL_1=#268BD2
COOL_2=#6C71C4
COOL_3=#D33682
COOL_4=#CB4B16
# -- alert pair -------------------------------------------------------------
COOL_HOT_0=#2AA198
COOL_HOT_4=#DC322F        # red
# -- off-ramp tints ---------------------------------------------------------
COOL_MINT=#859900         # green
COOL_BLUSH=#D33682        # magenta
# -- semantic aliases -------------------------------------------------------
COOL_ACCENT=#268BD2       # blue
COOL_ACTIVE=#2AA198       # cyan
COOL_URGENT=#DC322F       # red
COOL_WARN=#B58900         # yellow
COOL_GOOD=#859900         # green
COOL_INACTIVE=#586E75     # base01
